# Single source of truth for the Docker base image used by reproducible
# release builds AND the SDK pilot container. The release workflow reads
# this file and asserts the `FROM` lines of the production Dockerfile use
# `${image}@${digest}`; the docker-pilot-build workflow asserts the same
# for `lib/void-agent-sdk/Dockerfile.pilot`. Pinning every container to
# one committed digest means a rebuild from the same git SHA always pulls
# the same bytes.
#
# To rotate: pull the new tag, capture its digest, then update this file,
# the production Dockerfile FROM lines, and the pilot Dockerfile FROM line
# in one coordinated commit (CI fails closed if any drift apart).
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect node:22.12.0-slim --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}'
#
# CI fails the release/pilot build if any value drifts from this file.
image=node:22.12.0-slim
# Multi-arch manifest-list digest for node:22.12.0-slim as published by
# the official `node` library on Docker Hub. Buildx resolves this index
# to the per-arch image at build time, so the same digest pins both
# amd64 and arm64 builds against the same source-of-truth manifest.
# Rotated only with a coordinated commit that updates this file, the
# Dockerfile FROM line, and (typically) the .nvmrc Node version.
digest=sha256:35531c52ce27b6575d69755c73e65d4468dba93a25644eed56dc12879cae9213
